  },
  data: {
    LLM: "The Banker splits the deck into several face-down packets (typically 5 to 10) and keeps one Banker pile. Punters place bets on one or more packets. The top card of each packet and the Banker pile is revealed. Each punter wins if their chosen packet's top card ranks higher than the Banker's card; Banker wins ties. Winnings are paid out; then a new round may begin.",
    Player: "The Banker splits the deck into several face-down packets (typically 5 to 10) and keeps one Banker pile. Punters place bets on one or more packets. The top card of each packet and the Banker pile is revealed. Each punter wins if their chosen packet's top card ranks higher than the Banker's card; Banker wins ties. Winnings are paid out; then a new round may begin.",
    objective: "Bet on a packet that reveals a higher card than the Banker's card.",
    gameplay: "The Banker splits the deck into several face-down packets (typically 5 to 10) and keeps one Banker pile. Punters place bets on one or more packets. The top card of each packet and the Banker pile is revealed. Each punter wins if their chosen packet's top card ranks higher than the Banker's card; Banker wins ties. Winnings are paid out; then a new round may begin.",
    keyRules: [
      "Banker wins all ties. Punters bet on which packet will show a higher card than the Banker's card. Spread bets across packets to manage risk. Banker must have sufficient bankroll to cover all punter wins.",
